        "notes": "Separate (non-trap) findings: (1) Step 4 \"Norm preservation. Working over the same ground ring R, ||.|| is preserved\" asserts a norm on a generic commutative ring R without defining one, and the assembly line then silently switches from ||.|| to |.| \u2014 the step is the weakest link in an otherwise clean argument. (2) The closing display |tr_M(Phi_mass(beta))| = Vol(K_beta)/hbar_q^2 faithfully reproduces prop:topological-mass-formula, but BOTH disagree with the standing guardrail in AGENTS.md, which gives the per-knot mass as m(K) = m_e * Vol(K) * rho(K) / hbar_q^2 \u2014 the density factor rho(K) and the m_e scale are absent here. Reported as an upstream corpus tension, not as damage introduced by this block."
